# Skill & Reference Governance (Agent Requested)

## Principles

1. Local code, rules, DESIGN, CODEMAP beat external skills.
2. No duplicates; minimal import; transform to project context.
3. Record URL, license, date, purpose; no unapproved mass installs.
4. Classify: apply now / park as proposal / reject.

## Before import

1. Inventory `.cursor/rules/`, `.cursor/skills/`, `docs/`.
2. Score fitness: purpose, stack, ops, duplication, maintenance, security, a11y/perf, license, cost.
3. Pre-report and get approval for non-trivial imports.
4. Prefer `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` for procedures—do not copy into always-on rules.

## After import

Cite sources; note what was not applied; update CODEMAP/catalog if structure changed.

Catalog: `docs/references/GITHUB_STAR_CATALOG.md`  
Import skill: `.cursor/skills/external-skill-import/SKILL.md`  
Full Korean procedures/templates: `docs/pvc-guide/ko/core/03-skill-and-reference-governance.md`
